{"html":"<!DOCTYPE html>\n<html lang=\"en\">\n<head>\n<meta charset=\"utf-8\">\n<meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width,initial-scale=1\">\n<title>Path Points — Gradient Descent</title>\n<style>\n*{box-sizing:border-box}html,body{margin:0;width:100%;height:100%;overflow:hidden;background:#151719;font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;color:#f3f3f0}#root{position:relative;width:100%;height:100%;overflow:hidden;background:linear-gradient(135deg,#303336 0%,#1d2023 48%,#111416 100%)}.clip{position:absolute;inset:0}canvas{display:block;width:100%;height:100%}.scene{position:absolute;left:100px;top:170px;width:650px;opacity:0;transform-origin:left center}.eyebrow{font-size:25px;font-weight:700;letter-spacing:5px;color:#55e5ee;margin-bottom:30px}h1,h2{font-size:84px;line-height:1.04;letter-spacing:-4px;margin:0 0 35px;font-weight:700}h1 em,h2 em{font-style:normal;color:#ff6937}.description{font-size:31px;line-height:1.5;color:#c8cdd0;margin:0;max-width:630px}.rule{width:90px;height:5px;background:#ff6937;margin:32px 0}.equation{font-size:43px;letter-spacing:-1px;color:#55e5ee;padding:26px 0 20px}.detail{font-size:25px;line-height:1.5;color:#aab3b8;margin:15px 0 0}.uses{margin-top:32px;display:grid;gap:24px}.use{padding-left:24px;border-left:4px solid #ff6937}.use strong{display:block;font-size:32px;margin-bottom:7px}.use span{display:block;font-size:25px;line-height:1.35;color:#b9c1c5}.variants{display:grid;gap:21px;margin-top:29px}.variant{font-size:27px;color:#bdc6cb;line-height:1.4}.variant strong{color:#55e5ee;display:inline-block;min-width:165px}.footer{position:absolute;left:100px;bottom:75px;width:640px;font-size:24px;line-height:1.45;color:#9fa8ad;opacity:0}.accent{color:#ff865d}\n</style>\n</head>\n<body>\n<div id=\"root\" data-composition-id=\"main\" data-width=\"1920\" data-height=\"1080\" data-duration=\"36\">\n<div class=\"clip\" data-start=\"0\" data-duration=\"36\" data-track-index=\"0\"><canvas id=\"landscape\" width=\"1920\" height=\"1080\" aria-label=\"A three-dimensional loss surface with an orange ball following gradient-descent path points toward a cyan minimum marker.\"></canvas></div>\n<div class=\"clip\" data-start=\"0\" data-duration=\"36\" data-track-index=\"1\">\n<section class=\"scene\" data-scene=\"0\">\n<div class=\"eyebrow\">PATH POINTS</div>\n<h1>From crest<br>to <em>trough.</em></h1>\n<div class=\"rule\"></div>\n<p class=\"description\">Follow a ball downhill.<br>Each path point brings it closer to the bottom of a loss surface.</p>\n</section>\n<section class=\"scene\" data-scene=\"1\">\n<div class=\"eyebrow\">GRADIENT DESCENT</div>\n<h2>A first-order<br><em>optimizer.</em></h2>\n<p class=\"description\">It uses the loss gradient to update model parameters in the downhill direction.</p>\n<div class=\"equation\">θ next = θ − η ∇L(θ)</div>\n<p class=\"detail\">η is the learning rate: the size of a step.<br>∇L points toward the steepest increase.</p>\n</section>\n<section class=\"scene\" data-scene=\"2\" style=\"top:140px\">\n<div class=\"eyebrow\">MAJOR USE CASES</div>\n<h2>Learning by<br><em>reducing loss.</em></h2>\n<div class=\"uses\">\n<div class=\"use\"><strong>Neural networks</strong><span>Adjust weights during training.</span></div>\n<div class=\"use\"><strong>Regression &amp; classification</strong><span>Fit linear and logistic models.</span></div>\n<div class=\"use\"><strong>Recommendation systems</strong><span>Fit matrix-factorization models.</span></div>\n<div class=\"use\"><strong>Inverse problems</strong><span>Optimize reconstructions from observations.</span></div>\n</div>\n</section>\n<section class=\"scene\" data-scene=\"3\">\n<div class=\"eyebrow\">ONE IDEA, DIFFERENT UPDATES</div>\n<h2>Step closer.<br><em>Refine the fit.</em></h2>\n<p class=\"description\">Common variants differ in how much training data they use per update.</p>\n<div class=\"variants\">\n<div class=\"variant\"><strong>Batch</strong>All training examples</div>\n<div class=\"variant\"><strong>Stochastic</strong>One training example</div>\n<div class=\"variant\"><strong>Mini-batch</strong>A subset of examples</div>\n</div>\n</section>\n<div id=\"footer\" class=\"footer\"></div>\n</div>\n</div>\n<script src=\"gsap.min.js\"></script>\n<script>\n(function(){\n'use strict';\n// Editable composition settings. The surface and path are illustrative mathematics,\n// not measured model-training results. All visual state is a pure function of time.\nconst DURATION=36;\nconst C={orange:'#ff6937',cyan:'#55e5ee',white:'#f4f5f1',muted:'#aab5bb'};\nconst canvas=document.getElementById('landscape');\nconst ctx=canvas.getContext('2d');\nconst scenes=Array.from(document.querySelectorAll('.scene'));\nconst footer=document.getElementById('footer');\nconst clamp=(x,a=0,b=1)=>Math.max(a,Math.min(b,x));\nconst smooth=x=>{x=clamp(x);return x*x*(3-2*x);};\nconst mix=(a,b,t)=>a+(b-a)*t;\n// Convex demonstration surface: L(u,v)=0.13u²+0.009u⁴+0.10v².\nconst loss=(u,v)=>0.13*u*u+0.009*u*u*u*u+0.10*v*v;\nconst grad=(u,v)=>({u:0.26*u+0.036*u*u*u,v:0.20*v});\nconst project=(u,v,z=loss(u,v))=>({x:1340+(u-v)*85,y:655+(u+v)*53-z*40});\nconst path=[{u:-3.5,v:-1.25}];\nconst learningRate=0.36;\nfor(let i=0;i<28;i++){\n const p=path[path.length-1],g=grad(p.u,p.v);\n path.push({u:p.u-learningRate*g.u,v:p.v-learningRate*g.v});\n}\nconst cells=[];\nconst NX=38,NY=20;\nfor(let i=0;i<NX;i++)for(let j=0;j<NY;j++){\n const u=-3.8+i*7.6/NX,v=-1.9+j*3.8/NY;\n const du=7.6/NX,dv=3.8/NY;\n cells.push({u,v,du,dv,depth:u+v+(du+dv)/2});\n}\ncells.sort((a,b)=>a.depth-b.depth);\nfunction polygon(points,fill,stroke){\n ctx.beginPath();points.forEach((p,i)=>i?ctx.lineTo(p.x,p.y):ctx.moveTo(p.x,p.y));ctx.closePath();\n if(fill){ctx.fillStyle=fill;ctx.fill();}if(stroke){ctx.strokeStyle=stroke;ctx.stroke();}\n}\nfunction line(points,color,width){\n if(points.length<2)return;ctx.beginPath();points.forEach((p,i)=>i?ctx.lineTo(p.x,p.y):ctx.moveTo(p.x,p.y));\n ctx.strokeStyle=color;ctx.lineWidth=width;ctx.lineJoin='round';ctx.lineCap='round';ctx.stroke();\n}\nfunction ring(p,rx,ry,color,width){ctx.beginPath();ctx.ellipse(p.x,p.y,rx,ry,0,0,Math.PI*2);ctx.strokeStyle=color;ctx.lineWidth=width;ctx.stroke();}\nfunction text(str,x,y,size,color,align='left'){\n ctx.font=(size>=30?'600 ':'400 ')+size+'px Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif';ctx.textAlign=align;ctx.fillStyle=color;ctx.fillText(str,x,y);\n}\nfunction sceneAlpha(t,start,end,first,last){\n const enter=first?1:smooth((t-start)/0.7);\n const leave=last?1-smooth((t-35.1)/0.9):1-smooth((t-(end-0.65))/0.65);\n return enter*leave;\n}\nfunction draw(t){\n ctx.clearRect(0,0,1920,1080);\n const exit=1-smooth((t-35.1)/0.9);\n const reveal=mix(0.20,1,smooth(t/1.4))*exit;\n // Quiet backdrop illumination, drawn from fixed geometry.\n let glow=ctx.createRadialGradient(1390,570,25,1390,570,620);\n glow.addColorStop(0,'rgba(66,118,126,0.12)');glow.addColorStop(1,'rgba(0,0,0,0)');\n ctx.fillStyle=glow;ctx.fillRect(760,70,1160,940);\n ctx.save();ctx.globalAlpha=reveal;ctx.translate(0,28*(1-smooth(t/1.4)));\n // Ground plane provides a depth cue beneath the floating surface.\n for(let u=-4;u<=4;u+=0.5)line([project(u,-2.2,-0.65),project(u,2.2,-0.65)],'rgba(155,179,187,0.065)',1);\n for(let v=-2;v<=2;v+=0.5)line([project(-4,v,-0.65),project(4,v,-0.65)],'rgba(155,179,187,0.065)',1);\n // Thin boundary walls make the loss sheet read as a physical 3D object.\n const boundary=[[-3.8,-1.9],[3.8,-1.9],[3.8,1.9],[-3.8,1.9]];\n for(let k=0;k<4;k++){\n  const a=boundary[k],b=boundary[(k+1)%4];\n  polygon([project(a[0],a[1]),project(b[0],b[1]),project(b[0],b[1],loss(b[0],b[1])-0.13),project(a[0],a[1],loss(a[0],a[1])-0.13)],'#22292d');\n }\n // Painter-sorted mesh, shaded by height and the analytic surface slope.\n ctx.lineWidth=0.75;\n for(const cell of cells){\n  const {u,v,du,dv}=cell;\n  const h=loss(u+du/2,v+dv/2),g=grad(u+du/2,v+dv/2);\n  const lighting=clamp(0.57-0.14*g.u+0.06*g.v,0.20,0.93);\n  const valley=1-clamp(h/3.9);\n  const r=Math.round(31+lighting*39+valley*2);\n  const gr=Math.round(36+lighting*42+valley*12);\n  const b=Math.round(40+lighting*45+valley*15);\n  polygon([project(u,v),project(u+du,v),project(u+du,v+dv),project(u,v+dv)],'rgb('+r+','+gr+','+b+')','rgba(173,211,219,0.16)');\n }\n // Longer isolines reveal the continuous curvature of the sheet.\n for(const v of [-1.9,0,1.9]){\n  const pts=[];for(let i=0;i<=100;i++)pts.push(project(-3.8+i*7.6/100,v));\n  line(pts,v===0?'rgba(85,229,238,0.28)':'rgba(191,210,215,0.28)',v===0?1.7:1.2);\n }\n // Exact minimum and the fixed mathematical path.\n const minimum=project(0,0,0.03);\n ctx.save();ctx.shadowColor=C.cyan;ctx.shadowBlur=18;\n ring(minimum,24,12,C.cyan,2);ctx.restore();\n ring(minimum,7,3.5,'rgba(85,229,238,0.7)',1.5);\n const progress=clamp((t-2.7)/28.3)*(path.length-1);\n const index=Math.min(path.length-2,Math.floor(progress));\n const fraction=smooth(progress-index);\n const ball={u:mix(path[index].u,path[index+1].u,fraction),v:mix(path[index].v,path[index+1].v,fraction)};\n const projectedPath=path.map(p=>project(p.u,p.v,loss(p.u,p.v)+0.055));\n line(projectedPath,'rgba(85,229,238,0.26)',2);\n const active=projectedPath.slice(0,index+1);\n active.push(project(ball.u,ball.v,loss(ball.u,ball.v)+0.055));\n ctx.save();ctx.shadowColor=C.orange;ctx.shadowBlur=12;line(active,C.orange,3.5);ctx.restore();\n for(let i=0;i<path.length;i++){\n  const p=projectedPath[i];\n  // Later points converge tightly; alternating markers keep the endpoint legible.\n  if(i>12&&i%2)continue;\n  ctx.beginPath();ctx.arc(p.x,p.y,i<=index?4.5:3,0,Math.PI*2);\n  ctx.fillStyle=i<=index?C.orange:'rgba(85,229,238,0.47)';ctx.fill();\n }\n // Surface contact shadow and shaded orange sphere.\n const contact=project(ball.u,ball.v,loss(ball.u,ball.v)+0.04);\n ctx.save();ctx.translate(contact.x+3,contact.y+3);ctx.scale(1,0.45);\n let shadow=ctx.createRadialGradient(0,0,1,0,0,28);shadow.addColorStop(0,'rgba(0,0,0,0.65)');shadow.addColorStop(1,'rgba(0,0,0,0)');\n ctx.fillStyle=shadow;ctx.beginPath();ctx.arc(0,0,28,0,Math.PI*2);ctx.fill();ctx.restore();\n const bp={x:contact.x,y:contact.y-18};\n let sphere=ctx.createRadialGradient(bp.x-7,bp.y-8,2,bp.x+1,bp.y+2,22);\n sphere.addColorStop(0,'#ffe2b0');sphere.addColorStop(0.25,'#ff9a50');sphere.addColorStop(0.65,C.orange);sphere.addColorStop(1,'#9d2819');\n ctx.save();ctx.shadowColor='rgba(255,105,55,0.35)';ctx.shadowBlur=25;\n ctx.fillStyle=sphere;ctx.beginPath();ctx.arc(bp.x,bp.y,20,0,Math.PI*2);ctx.fill();ctx.restore();\n // Readable leaders identify the start and the trough without covering the path.\n const start=projectedPath[0];\n const startAlpha=1-smooth((t-8)/2);\n ctx.save();ctx.globalAlpha*=startAlpha;\n line([{x:start.x-12,y:start.y-30},{x:start.x-55,y:start.y-75},{x:start.x-145,y:start.y-75}],'rgba(255,135,92,0.75)',1.5);\n text('CREST',start.x-145,start.y-91,25,'#ff9b72');ctx.restore();\n const troughAlpha=mix(0.45,1,smooth((t-19)/6));\n ctx.save();ctx.globalAlpha*=troughAlpha;\n line([{x:minimum.x+28,y:minimum.y+8},{x:minimum.x+96,y:minimum.y+72},{x:minimum.x+225,y:minimum.y+72}],'rgba(85,229,238,0.65)',1.5);\n text('TROUGH',minimum.x+105,minimum.y+58,25,C.cyan);\n text('Minimum of this surface',minimum.x+105,minimum.y+107,23,C.muted);ctx.restore();\n // The progress caption reflects the visible action, rather than a fabricated metric.\n const caption=t<7?'A high starting point':t<17?'Follow the negative gradient':t<28?'Successive updates reduce the loss':'Approaching the minimum';\n line([{x:925,y:929},{x:1780,y:929}],'rgba(163,185,192,0.20)',1);\n ctx.beginPath();ctx.arc(929,978,5,0,Math.PI*2);ctx.fillStyle=C.orange;ctx.fill();\n text(caption,951,987,29,'#d5dcdf');\n ctx.restore();\n // Text transitions are seek-safe and act on content, never on clip visibility.\n const timing=[[0,7],[7,17],[17,27],[27,36]];\n scenes.forEach((el,i)=>{\n  const a=sceneAlpha(t,timing[i][0],timing[i][1],i===0,i===3);\n  el.style.opacity=String(a);\n  const enter=i===0?smooth(t/0.85):smooth((t-timing[i][0])/0.7);\n  el.style.transform='translateY('+(20*(1-enter))+'px)';\n });\n const note=t<7?'An illustrative, smooth loss landscape.':t<17?'An optimization method used to train ML models.':t<27?'These applications can use gradient-based optimization.':'Near this trough, the gradient approaches zero. Other loss landscapes can contain local minima.';\n footer.textContent=note;\n let fa=0;timing.forEach((pair,i)=>fa=Math.max(fa,sceneAlpha(t,pair[0],pair[1],i===0,i===3)));\n footer.style.opacity=String(fa*0.95);\n}\nconst playhead={t:0};\nconst timeline=gsap.timeline({paused:true});\ntimeline.to(playhead,{t:DURATION,duration:DURATION,ease:'none',onUpdate:function(){draw(playhead.t);}},0);\nwindow.__timelines=window.__timelines||{};\nwindow.__timelines['main']=timeline;\ndraw(0);\n})();\n</script>\n</body>\n</html>","width":1920,"height":1080,"duration_seconds":36,"assumptions":["Chose a silent 36-second, 16:9 educational animation because duration, audio and aspect ratio were unspecified.","The ball follows computed gradient-descent updates on an illustrative convex mathematical surface; it does not represent measured training results.","The editable 3D landscape uses a projected Canvas mesh, with volcanic orange, cyan and gray shading.","All artwork is procedural; no external assets, fonts or associated license gaps are involved. GSAP is supplied locally by the harness.","This source has not been rendered or visually reviewed."],"missing_inputs":[],"summary":"Standalone editable animation showing a ball descending toward a trough, with explanations of gradient descent, major applications and update variants."}